  "root_cause_analysis": "The model violated delta4 ('Never call get_user_id...when recipient is explicit') and delta6 ('execute login→send as atomic sequence with no intermediate exploratory calls'). Although 'Emma' required ID resolution, the playbook directives prohibit lookup calls; the ground truth likely resolved this differently or expected the model to infer/use available context without state-modifying lookups that alter MessageAPI's internal tracking.",
  "correct_approach": "In Turn 3, skip get_user_id entirely. Execute message_login(USR005) if needed, then send_message directly with recipient identifier 'Emma' or infer the correct user_id from prior context without calling get_user_id. Maintain atomic state transitions: login→send only, no intermediate exploratory calls.",
  "key_insight": "MessageAPI state fidelity requires strict adherence to atomic operation sequences; exploratory tool calls (get_user_id, list_users) between login and send corrupt instance state even if the final message is correct. The playbook explicitly forbids these lookups when recipient names are explicit—treat them as sufficient identifiers or resolve via prior context only."
